{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793018588,"nonce":"LINvq4g+DOJ2N91QicmDClD1gxo=","title":"Studio: expose versioned component and layout inspection data","message":"Status: planned; implementation has not started.\n\nParent: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\nProgram epic: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\nCross-repository integration: RayDE:c299bb980e54d48d600312f31a178213d13bc56bc2d3967c4bf42ef9816d6671\nPhase: 1\n\nScope\nExpose component identity separately from rendered layout nodes: hierarchy, stable generation-scoped IDs, readable typed props, explicit versus computed layout/style values, bounds, transforms and inspectable state. Snapshot/delta data must be bounded and serializable; omit opaque native pointers, closures and secret runtime-service state. Track removed nodes and require generation checks for selections and updates.\n\nAcceptance\nAn inspector consumer can rebuild the correct hierarchy across reactive child changes without dereferencing runtime pointers. Unsupported/cyclic/large values have bounded summaries. Selection IDs become invalid when their generation or node is gone; snapshots and deltas have compatibility tests.\n\nDepends on\n- ashui:be85b726001078af0db7f8ed83dae64d5b7ad267e941306e498e3ec3f1b6397e — Studio: expose typed component mounting and isolated preview contexts\n- RayDE:03d642c635db571275ac33007da36ac479d027a08d48d0f0a08680788c7ac2d0 — Studio: choose preview compiler, runtime and isolation contract\n\nKeep implementation and validation evidence in this tracker. Follow the parent gate decisions; link any additional concrete runtime/backend prerequisite discovered by the feasibility work. No cloud deployment or new backend language is implied by this planning issue.","files":null}]}